“STORM OF STRANDS” (15s, 9:16, 30fps)

REFERENCE: Uploaded Image

STYLE
filigree-fiber creatures · flowing ribbon physics · hyper-real materials · iridescent silk · volumetric strand-vortex · dream-storm atmosphere

PHYSICS
• Strand bundles bend, whip, and ripple with simulated turbulence
• Fine fibers peel off and rejoin like fluid ribbons
• Color streams (yellow, red, teal) react to airflow
• Dustlike particles drift between strands
• Iridescent glints on curves and spirals
• Subtle body-breathing motion beneath the strands

CAMERA
Many shots · fast cuts · micro-movements · quick arcs · bold push-ins · no locked-off frames.
Always moving · expressive arcs · close-ups → wide reveals → tracking shots
Macro DOF for texture moments, then dramatic lens shifts.

SCENE SEQUENCE

S1 — Birth Swirl (0.0–2.0s)

Extreme close-ups of swirling strands forming the horse’s face. The ribbon-fibers of the horse flutter violently, like thousands of flexible strands snapping in turbulent wind. Micro-vibrations, iridescent sheen, visible depth.
Camera circles, macro detailing. Ribbons snap into place like magnetic silk.

S2 — Head Lift (2.0–4.0s)

The horse lifts its head.
Huge wind pushes the strands backward.
Camera low and rising, emphasizing scale.

S3 — Strand Storm (4.0–6.0s)

A whirlpool of loose filaments erupts around it, spinning like a tornado of multi-colored fibers.
Camera does a fast crescent-orbit.

S4 — The Step (6.0–8.5s)

The horse takes a slow, powerful step.
Ground ripples with ribbon-like shockwaves.
Cinematic handheld shake.

S5 — Full Reveal (8.5–11.0s)

Wide shot.
The entire creature stands in a swirling, luminous storm of its own strands.
Fiber particles drift like glowing snow.

S6 — Charge Forward (11.0–14.5s)

The horse suddenly bursts into motion.
Strand-trails whip behind it like comet tails.
Camera tracking alongside, fast, dynamic.

S7 — Title Pulse (14.5–15.0s)

Black screen.
Soft glowing letters appear:
“STORM OF STRANDS”
A faint wind-filament hum plays.